;; clj-kondo configuration for glitter-gl.
;;
;; jolt.ffi/defcfn defines a var per bound C symbol. clj-kondo cannot see
;; through the macro, so hooks/jolt_ffi.clj rewrites each call into an
;; equivalent `defn` — see that file for why. Without it every gl-*/gtk-*
;; binding in glitter-gl.gl / glitter-gl.gtk is a false "Unresolved symbol".
;;
;; The verbatim-ported library layer (glimmer-gl's geometry/matrix/shader/GL
;; modules, namespace-renamed only — see NOTICE.md's porting ledger and the
;; Standard Verbatim Port Procedure in the port plan, private planning
;; store) carries a handful of inherited clj-kondo
;; findings from upstream: shadowed core names (min/max/identity — deliberate
;; in the original thi.ng/geom-derived design), an unresolved clojure.math
;; require (a false positive — glitter-gl.vec2/heading resolves and runs
;; correctly under Jolt; clj-kondo's clojure.math stub just doesn't know
;; about Jolt's own math namespace), an unresolved glitter-gl.matrix
;; reference in quaternion_test.clj (also a false positive — it resolves
;; transitively through quaternion.clj's own require), a couple of unused
;; `vec3`/`testing` refers, and a few redundant-expression style notes. Every
;; one of these is confirmed identical to glimmer-gl's own source via the
;; Standard Verbatim Port Procedure's diff check — "fixing" any of them here
;; would mean deviating from a file this project's whole porting discipline
;; depends on staying byte-for-byte identical to upstream. This is the same
;; call glitter's own .clj-kondo/config.edn makes for its Replicant-ported
;; files (see that file's :output :exclude-files comment): permanent,
;; harmless, out-of-scope findings for a deliberate porting strategy, not
;; defects to silently patch around.
{:hooks {:analyze-call {jolt.ffi/defcfn hooks.jolt-ffi/defcfn}}
 :output
 {:exclude-files
  ["glitter_gl/(vector|vec2|matrix|quaternion|aabb|rect|circle|line|plane|triangle|sphere|polygon|bezier|intersect|mesh|glmesh|primitives|polyhedra|shader|gl|offscreen|renderer)\\.clj$"
   "glitter_gl/(vector|vec2|matrix|quaternion|aabb|rect|circle|line|plane|triangle|sphere|polygon|bezier|intersect|mesh|glmesh|primitives|polyhedra|shader|gl|offscreen)_test\\.clj$"]}}
